    "result_text": "The build is green.\n\nI implemented the email-uniqueness rule following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern, mirroring the existing duplicate-telephone rule:\n\n- **`RejectDuplicateOwnerEmail`** \u2014 a single-responsibility step that runs after `NormalizeOwnerEmail` (so the request email is already trimmed/lower-cased). It skips absent emails, and rejects when the normalized request email matches any existing owner's email normalized the same way. It reuses the existing `OwnerEmails` helper (`isPresent`/`normalize`) rather than duplicating that logic, keeping the comparison case-insensitive as the spec requires.\n- **`DuplicateEmailException`** \u2014 a checked exception (extends `Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause and the escalation machinery can catch it.\n- **`DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler`** + escalation YAML \u2014 responds `409 Conflict` with a `ProblemDetail`, exactly like the telephone/household handlers.\n- Wired `rejectDuplicateEmail` into `owners.POST.yml` between `normalizeEmail` and `build`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` and the full suite pass.",
